details:
(a) whether Government has taken note of reports indicating that nearly 97 per cent of mobile subscribers receive spam calls daily, with a majority originating from mobile numbers rather than registered enterprise numbers;
(b) the number of complaints relating to Unsolicited Commercial Communications (UCC), spam calls and spam SMSs received during the last five years, year-wise, along with the number of complaints resolved and action taken thereon; and
(c) the number of mobile connections, telemarketers, entities and telecom resources disconnected, suspended or blacklisted for violating UCC regulations during the last five years, year-wise?

(a) State-wise number of primary school teachers appointed before 23 August 2010 who are presently required to qualify Teacher Eligibility Test (TET) by 31 August, 2028;
(b) whether Government has assessed the number of teachers with more than 15–30 years of service whose employment may be jeopardised if they do not to qualify TET by 31 August, 2028, if so, details thereof;
(c) how many representations has the Ministry received from teachers' associations and State Governments seeking exemption for pre-2010 teachers, and action taken thereon; and
(d) whether any proposal is under consideration to safeguard the service security of teachers appointed before 23 August, 2010?

(a) the current hospital bed availability in the country per 1,000 population;
(b) the number of Primary Health Centres (PHCs) functioning without a doctor;
(c) the shortage of specialists at Community Health Centres (CHCs); and
(d) the typical bed occupancy rate in many Government hospitals?

(a) whether business procurement in LIC is a collective responsibility of all marketing officials including Development Officers (Class-II), ABM, BM, SBM, CM, MM, SDM and RM;
(b) whether Development Officers appointed under the LIC Staff Rules, 1960 are permanent employees, if so, under what statutory provisions they can be terminated or penalised solely for business performance;
(c) whether many Development Officers with over 20–30 years of service have not received time-bound promotions, if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the details of official vehicles, fuel reimbursement, laptops and related facilities for ABM to RM, including annual expenditure, post-wise?

(a) the total number of applications for compassionate appointment received by Western Coalfields Limited from 2012 till date, year-wise;
(b) the number of compassionate appointment applications approved, rejected and pending by Western Coalfields Limited from 2012 till date, year-wise; and
(c) whether any applications for compassionate appointment in Western Coalfields Limited pertain to the dependents of employees who died in the year 2012, if so, the number of such applications, the present status and the reasons for the delay or non-disposal?

(a) total number of beneficiaries approved under the Production Linked Incentive Scheme for Food Processing Industry (PLISFPI) including number of MSMEs and large enterprises, 
(b) whether there is any gap between the total scheme outlay and the incentives disbursed so far;
(c) total amount of incentives disbursed under the Scheme till date including MSMEs;
(d) the total number of direct and indirect jobs generated under the Scheme against the prescribed employment target, State/UT-wise, category wise; and
(e) the total additional processing capacity created, incremental sales achieved and exports generated by beneficiary companies under the Scheme, since 2021, year-wise?

(a) the country-wise details of foreign visits undertaken by the Prime Minister since 2021;
(b) the total expenditure incurred on such visit since 2021, year-wise and visit-wise; and
(c) the country-wise details of bilateral agreements/MoUs signed during these visits, the investment commitments announced, and the actual Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) received in India as a result thereof?

(a) number of new National Highway and Expressway projects awarded, completed and opened to traffic during the last two years, State-wise, total length (km) and project cost;
(b) number of National Highways and Expressway projects that developed potholes, cracks or other defects within one year of construction for the above period, State-wise;
(c) details of name of the projects, date of completion, project cost and length (km);
(d) number of road accidents, injuries, fatalities, traffic disruptions and vehicle damage reported as a consequence of such defects for the said period; and
(e) action taken against contractors or agencies responsible for such defects?

(a) reasons Government has virtually withdrawn regular petrol from retail outlets, denying consumers particularly owners of older vehicles the freedom to choose fuel compatible with their vehicles;
(b) whether Government has assessed that claimed savings in crude oil imports are being offset by increased fuel consumption resulting from lower mileage, details on net foreign exchange savings;
(c) whether Government has assessed the additional financial burden on consumers due to reduced mileage following mandatory rollout of E20 petrol, details thereof; and
(d) who will compensate consumers if their vehicles suffer damage or loss of performance despite assurances by automobile manufacturers regarding safety of E20 petrol?

(a) whether over ?100 crore worth of railway linen has reportedly gone missing in just four years and whether the Ministry has fixed responsibility for these losses; 
(b) whether the Ministry has the reasons for losses are primarily due to theft, contractor lapses, or administrative negligence; 
(c) whether the cost of missing linen is recovered from onboard attendants or housekeeping staff through deductions from their wages, if so, the quantum of money recovered during the last five years; and 
(d) the reasons for non-adoption of the digital inventory systems by Indian Railways to track linen as used in hotels, hospitals and airlines?

(a) whether Government is aware of reports that large quantities of bedsheets, blankets, towels, pillows and other linen supplied in AC coaches have been stolen, causing significant financial losses to Railways;
(b) total quantity and estimated value of such items reported missing and financial loss incurred during last five years, zone-wise;
(c) whether any assessment has been made regarding impact of these losses on passenger amenities and railway expenditure; 
(d)whether repeated shortage of linen has been flagged in internal audits/inspection reports, if so, the finding thereof and action taken thereon; and
(e) measures taken to prevent thefts, fix accountability and strengthen monitoring of linen inventory in trains?

(a) whether families are advised to arrange private lawyers in respective countries in cases involving missing or detained Indian nationals abroad;
(b) whether Government has assessed the financial and practical difficulties faced by middle-class and economically weaker families in engaging lawyers and travelling abroad to pursue such cases;
(c) whether Government proposes to provide free or subsidised legal representation through Indian Embassies/Consulates in deserving cases, particularly where families are unable to bear the cost of legal proceedings abroad; and
(d) the details of legal and financial assistance provided through the Indian Community Welfare Fund (ICWF) during the last five years, country-wise?

(a) the total area of forest land diverted for non-forest purposes and the total number of trees permitted to be felled during the last five years, year-wise, State-wise and project-wise, indicating the purpose of diversion;
(b) the names of the top 50 projects involving the highest extent of forest land diversion and tree felling during the said period, indicating the area diverted, number of trees felled, user agency and present status of each project; and
(c) whether Government has assessed the net loss of forest cover and carbon sequestration resulting from forest diversion for infrastructure projects and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total number of incidents of attacks and atrocities against members of the Scheduled Castes reported under the Scheduled Castes (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989 during the last five years and the current year, year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) category-wise details of such incidents, including murder, attempt to murder, rape, gang rape, grievous hurt, social boycott, public humiliation, caste-based abuse and other offences, State-wise/UT-wise for the said period; and
(c) number of cases in which FIRs were registered, chargesheets filed, arrests made, convictions secured and cases are pending investigation or trial, State-wise/UT-wise as on date?

(a) the total number of registered cooperative societies in the country, category-wise and State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) the number of cooperative societies that are presently functional, non-functional, under liquidation and dissolved, State-wise/UT-wise;
(c) the number of cooperative societies that are profit-making, loss-making, and those for which financial information is not available, State-wise/UT-wise; and
(d) the reasons for the large number of non-functional and financially distressed cooperative societies and the corrective measures taken by Government to revive them?

(a) total quantity of foodgrains procured, stored and available with Food Corporation of India (FCI) as on date, indicating quantity stored in silos, covered godowns and Cover and Plinth (CAP) storage, respectively;
(b) the quantity of foodgrains that has deteriorated or become unfit for human consumption during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise, along with reasons;
(c) whether Government proposes to phase out CAP storage and augment scientific storage infrastructure, including silos and mechanised warehouses, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government has considered distributing surplus foodgrain free of cost or at subsidised rates to poor and vulnerable families instead of allowing stocks to deteriorate, the details thereof?

(a) current status of the rollout of smart electricity meters under the Revamped Distribution Sector Scheme (RDSS), indicating the number of smart meters sanctioned, installed and made operational against fixed targets and reasons for delays, if any State-wise and Union Territory-wise;
(b) whether Government has received complaints regarding inaccurate billing, excessive charges, technical malfunctions, faulty meter readings or other consumer grievances relating to smart electricity meters during the last three years, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) steps taken by Government to enhance transparency, consumer confidence and accountability in implementation of the smart metering programme?

(a) the total number of airports that have been newly constructed in the country since 2021, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) the total number of such newly constructed airports that have been inaugurated by the Hon'ble Prime Minister since 2021, along with dates of inauguration and States/UTs; and
(c) out of the airports referred to in parts (a) and (b), the number of airports that are presently operational, non-operational and closed, respectively, along with the reasons for the non-operational or closed status of each such airport?

(a) whether the Ministry is aware that passengers are often unable to obtain confirmed sleeper class tickets because the number of AC coaches has increased while sleeper and general coaches have not kept pace with demand;
(b) the average waiting list for sleeper class compared to AC class on major routes;
(c) number of sleeper and general coaches which have been replaced by AC coaches during the last five years; and
(d) whether Government will fix a minimum number of sleeper and general coaches in long-distance trains to protect affordable travel for ordinary passengers?

(a) whether the Department-related Parliamentary Standing Committee on Agriculture, Animal Husbandry and Food Processing recommended implementation of a legally binding Minimum Support Price (MSP), if so, the details of the recommendations;
(b) whether Government has examined the recommendations of the Committee, if so, the present status of each recommendation and the action taken thereon;
(c) whether Government proposes to implement a legally binding MSP, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the timeline, if any, fixed by Government for taking a final decision on the recommendations of the Committee?

(a) whether Government would provide the estimated number of unemployed persons in the country till date, State/UT-wise;
(b) the details of unemployment rate (in percentage) during each of the last three years, gender-wise and age group-wise (15–29 years, 30–44 years, 45–59 years and 60 years & above); and
(c) the number of jobs created/provided against the Prime Minister's commitment to create two crore jobs annually since its announcement, year-wise?

(a) whether Central Government civilian employees who retired during the period from 2006 to 2008 under the Sixth Central Pay Commission (6th CPC) have not been granted benefits of the Modified Assured Career Progression (MACP) scheme and if so, the reasons therefor;
(b) the number of civilian employees who retired during the said period and were deprived of the benefit of MACP scheme, department-wise; and
(c) whether Government has issued any Office Memoranda (OMs) for grant of MACP benefits, arrears and revised pensionary benefits to civilian employees retired during that period and if so, the details thereof including the implementation timeline?

(a) whether Government has received any proposal, including the resolution passed by the Telangana Legislative Assembly for inclusion of Gor Boli, the mother tongue of the Banjara community, in the Eighth Schedule to the Constitution;
(b) if so, the details thereof and the present status of the proposal;
(c) whether Government proposes to include Gor Boli in the Eighth Schedule, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken by Government for the preservation and promotion of Gor Boli and Banjara culture?

(a) whether Government has examined the demand for uniform recognition of the Banjara community, including its recognised synonyms, as Scheduled Tribes across the country, in the light of recommendations of the Kaka Kalelkar Commission, U.N. Dhebar Commission, Lokur Commission, Chanda Commission, Renke Commission, Idate Commission, the Joint Parliamentary Committee and the observations of the Punjab and Haryana High Court;
(b) if so, details thereof and present status of the matter;
(c) whether consultations have been held with the Registrar General of India, the National Commission for Scheduled Tribes and the concerned State Governments in this regard; and
(d) actions taken on the recommendations?

(a) whether any representations have been received from contractual employees of WAPCOS Limited during the last five years seeking regularisation of their service conditions, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the action taken by Government and WAPCOS Limited on such representations; and
(c) the steps taken to improve the job security, service conditions, welfare and motivation of long-serving contractual employees engaged in the implementation of water sector projects?

(a) the objectives, timelines and phase-wise targets of BharatNet project, including number of Gram Panchayats and villages connected under Phases I, II and III;
(b) whether the project has missed multiple deadlines in 2014, 2015, 2019 and 2023 and 2025 and if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) the funds allocated, revised, released and actual expenditure incurred under BharatNet project since inception, year-wise and phase-wise;
(d) the State/UT-wise details of utilisation of funds and the reasons for under-utilisation, if any; and
(e) the number of villages and Gram Panchayats where fibre has been laid but broadband services are not operational, along with the reasons therefor?
v

(a) total Budget Estimates (BE), Revised Estimate (RE), Actual Expenditure (AE) under the Scheme for Rehabilitation of Manual Scavengers (SRMS) during last five financial years, year-wise, State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) whether Government has discontinued explicit rehabilitation components such as compensation, cash assistance, skill development and concessional loans after replacing SRMS with National Action for Mechanised Sanitation Ecosystem (NAMASTE) scheme;
(c) total funds allocated, released, utilised under NAMASTE during last five years, year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise;
(d) amount of financial assistance provided through National Safai Karamcharis Finance & Development Corporation (NSKFDC) during last five years, year-wise, State-wise/UT-wise; and
(e) total number of manual scavengers identified, rehabilitated and provided compensation for above period, State-wise?
SR

(a) the details of MoU signed between the Delhi Police and the 'Sahakar Taxi Cooperative' and whether it has a provision for the protection of the employment of the 148 employees working for the last 40 years;
(b) the number of new employees recruited in the organization till date;
(c) the statutory and financial basis for the new appointments, when the existing employees were laid off on grounds of 'losses', given that this service operates on a 'no-profit, no-loss' basis; and
(d) the basis for retrenchment in the name of a financial deficit when the DoPT has deemed their work to be of a regular nature?

(a) total Budget Estimates (BE), RE, AE under MGNREGA from 2021–22 till date, year-wise;
(b) total number of days of employment guaranteed and actual average number of days of employment provided per household under MGNREGA during said period, year-wise;
(c) total amount of wage payments presently pending under MGNREGA, State-wise;
(d) total financial outlay of the proposed VB G-RAM G framework providing 125 days of guaranteed employment;
(e) whether the budgetary allocation proposed under VB G-RAM G is proportionate to the financial requirement for providing 125 days of guaranteed employment to all eligible households; and
(f) estimated additional fiscal burden on States under the 60:40 sharing model?

(a) total number of mega food parks sanctioned, completed, operational, cancelled and non-functional under the Mega Food Park Scheme (MFPS) since its inception, State-wise;
(b) whether it is a fact that the mandatory requirement of 50 acres of contiguous land led to significant delays in project execution and cancellation of several projects;
(c) number of projects that faced delays due to non-availability of land, bank loan refusals and failure to meet staged subsidy conditions; and
(d) total funds allocated, released and actually utilised under the scheme, year-wise since inception?

(a) whether it is a fact that Denotified, Nomadic and Semi-Nomadic Tribes (DNTs/NTs/SNTs) are presently not recognized as a separate constitutional category under Articles 15(4), 15(5) and 16(4) of the Constitution of India, despite being historically stigmatized under the Criminal Tribes Acts;
(b) whether Government admits that the continued forced dispersion of DNTs across SC, ST, OBC and open categories has resulted in systemic exclusion, denial of representation and erosion of targeted welfare; and
(c) if so, the legal justification for not creating a distinct and exclusive classification for DNTs, despite repeated recommendations of national commissions and judicial observations on substantive equality?

(a) whether it is a fact that Denotified, Nomadic and Semi-nomadic tribes (DNTs/NTs/SNTs) have never been separately enumerated in any decennial Census of the country;
(b) whether Government proposes to include DNTs as a separate enumerated category in the forthcoming Census 2027, so as to generate reliable data on population, education, housing and livelihood; and
(c) if not, the reasons for denying DNTs the data-based governance that forms the foundation of welfare planning and affirmative action?

(a) the total number of off-grid standalone solar pumps installed under the PM-KUSUM scheme (Component B) since its launch in 2019 and the year-wise budget allocations, actual releases and utilisation of these funds;
(b) the actual utilisation data of these solar pumps based on reports of remote monitoring system (RMS), including days of operation per year and solar energy generated versus utilised;
(c) whether it is a fact that a significant proportion of these pumps remain idle for half the year or more, leading to under-utilisation of installed solar capacity and if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the State-wise details of utilisation rates?

(a) whether the Food Corporation of India (FCI) lost about 50,000 tonnes of foodgrains during transit between April–December Financial Year 2025-26, the resulting monetary loss to the exchequer;
(b) the details of such transit losses, including losses attributed to spillage, theft, poor infrastructure and handling deficiencies, State-wise and route-wise;
(c) whether transit losses stood at 73,000 tonnes in Financial Year 2024-25;
(d) how many beneficiary families under NFSA could have been fed with the quantity lost; and
(e) whether any accountability has been fixed in cases of abnormal losses and the details thereof?

(a) total funds allocated, released, utilised under the Namami Gange Programme since its inception, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) State-wise and project-wise details of the sanctioned projects, including cost of each project, amount released so far, expenditure incurred, physical progress and expected date of completion;
(c) total amount of unspent balance currently lying with implementing agencies, State Governments and executing bodies, year -wise and State-wise;
(d) whether any projects have faced cost escalation, time overruns or re-tendering and the details thereof; and
(e) the mechanism in place for independent third-party audit of fund utilisation and outcome verification?

(a) number of farmers insured under Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) as on date, State/UT-wise;
(b) total premium amount collected during the last five years, State-wise;
(c) number of claims reported, approved and settled under PMFBY for the said period, State/UT-wise;
(d) total amount of insurance claims paid to farmers and total amount pending for settlement as on date, State/UT-wise;
(e) number of cases where farmers received extremely low compensation amounts such as ?1 to ?5, State-wise; and
(f) whether any inquiry has been conducted into irregularities in crop damage assessment and claim calculation, if so, action taken against erring officials or insurance companies?

(a) the details of budget allocated, RE, AE incurred by the Ministry from 2021-22 till date;
(b) the amount approved, transferred and utilised under the Compensatory Afforestation Fund (CAMPA), State/UT-wise during the above period including details of States that have utilised less than 50 per cent and less than 25 per cent of allocated funds;
(c) the year-wise allocation and actual expenditure under the Green India Mission (GIM); and
(d) whether key climate adaptation programmes such as the National Adaptation Fund (NAF), Climate Change Action Plan (CCAP) and National Mission on Himalayan Studies (NMHS) have been shifted to "non-scheme" categories without clear budget allocation since 2022-23 and if so, the reasons therefor?

(a) the Budget Estimates (BE), RE, AE under NESIDS - Other Than Roads Infrastructure (OTRI) from 2022–23 till date;
(b) the percentage utilisation of funds (actual vs RE) for the above period;
(c) the number of projects approved under NESIDS–OTRI as on date, State/UT-wise and sector-wise;
(d) the total cost and actual expenditure for each completed and ongoing project under NESIDS–OTRI, State/UT-wise; and
(e) whether Government has reviewed the variation in BE and RE during the years?

(a) total budgetary allocation made under the Scheduled Caste Sub Plan (SCSP) and details on both targeted and non-targeted schemes, during each of the last five financial years, scheme-wise, year-wise and State-wise/Union Territory-wise;
(b) Revised Estimates (RE) for such allocations during the same period, scheme-wise, year-wise and State-wise/Union Territory-wise; and
(c) actual expenditure incurred under these targeted and non-targeted schemes during the last five years, scheme-wise, year-wise and State-wise/Union Territory-wise?

(a) the total number of Free Trade Agreements (FTAs) and Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreements (CEPAs) signed by India so far, country-wise since 2020;
(b) the country wise details of India’s total exports and imports in terms of value (? crore), volume and major commodities traded, since the year of implementation of FTAs/CEPAs year-wise;
(c) the year-wise trade balance (surplus/deficit) with each of the above countries from the year of agreement till date; and
(d) whether Government has conducted any impact assessment of these FTAs/CEPAs on India’s trade deficit?

(a) the total budgetary allocation made for National Mission on Natural Farming (NMNF) since inception, year-wise;
(b) the total funds released to States/UTs and the actual expenditure incurred thereunder, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(c) the total number of farmers enrolled under the Mission so far, State/UT-wise;
(d) the total number of farmers who have received the incentive of ?4,000 per acre per year under the Mission, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(e) the total area (in hectares/acreage) for which ?4,000 per acre incentive has been disbursed, year-wise and State/UT-wise; and
(f) whether all eligible farmers enrolled under the scheme have received the incentive, if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of job seekers registered and vacancies mobilised on National Career Service (NCS) portal during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the number of candidates who were provisionally shortlisted/selected through the portal and job fairs during that period, year-wise;
(c) the number of candidates who have actually secured final employment/placement through the portal during that period, year-wise;
(d) whether Government proposes to introduce a mandatory reporting mechanism for employers and job seekers to update final hiring status to ensure transparency; and
(e) whether any third-party audit or impact assessment has been conducted to evaluate the actual placement rate of registered job seekers and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether, despite the admission to MBBS and AYUSH courses is conducted through the common NEET examination, different norms have been applied regarding the conduct of the National Exit Test (NExT) examinations;
(b) whether NExT for MBBS graduates has been deferred due to lack of adequate preparedness and infrastructure;
(c) whether, despite similar concerns relating to infrastructure and preparedness, a compulsory exit examination has been implemented for AYUSH students of the 2021 to 2023 batches; and
(d) the reasons for not extending similar relief to AYUSH students as granted to MBBS students?

(a) whether it is a fact that dues amounting to about ?8.1 lakh crore are currently locked due to delayed payments to MSMEs, as highlighted in the Economic Survey 2025–26;
(b) total outstanding dues payable to MSMEs by Ministries, CPSEs and State entities as on date, Ministry/PSU-wise and average time taken for settlement of such dues;
(c) total number of cases filed on the MSME Online Dispute Resolution (ODR) Portal since its launch;
(d) details on the total amount involved in these cases; and
(e) whether Government acknowledges that persistent delayed payments continue to pose a serious challenge to the working capital position of MSMEs?

(a) whether it is a fact that several Schemes/Missions announced in successive Budgets, including the PM-eBus Sewa Scheme, the National Urban Digital Mission, the Urban Challenge Fund and the Scheme for Industrial Housing, witnessed delays in finalisation of guidelines, Cabinet approval and actual utilisation of funds;
(b) the year-wise Budget Estimates (BE), Revised Estimates (RE) and Actual Expenditure incurred under each of the above Schemes since their announcement; and
(c) the total funds allocated, released and actually spent under each Scheme so far, scheme-wise and year-wise?

(a) the State/UT-wise number of trees planted under Ek Ped Maa Ke Naam campaign;
(b) the progress made against the target of 140 crore trees by 31 March, 2025;
(c) the survival and mortality rate of saplings planted;
(d) the funds allocated, released and utilized in this regard; and
(e) the details of audits conducted and deficiencies noticed?

(a) Budget Estimates (BE), Revised Estimates (RE) and Actual Expenditure incurred under the Scheduled Caste Sub-Plan / Scheduled Caste Development budget for during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) scheme-wise and Ministry/Department-wise details of the above allocations, indicating the funds earmarked under targeted SC-specific schemes and non-targeted or general schemes claiming SC components;
(c) percentage share of Scheduled Caste allocations in the total Union Budget in each of the above years; and
(d) year-wise utilisation gap between BE, RE and Actual Expenditure during the said period and the reasons for shortfall or diversion?

(a) list of States/Union Territories where Panchayat elections were delayed beyond the constitutional deadline of five years along with the original due date, last election date and the current status of pending polls for Gram Panchayats, Block Panchayats and Zilla Parishads;
(b) number of Panchayat bodies (Gram Panchayats, Block Panchayats and Zila Parishads) whose tenure expired without fresh elections as on date, with State-wise/UT-wise; and
(c) the amount of Central grants under schemes such as 15th Finance Commission and other rural development funds that has been withheld or not released due to these delayed Panchayat elections, State-wise and year-wise details thereof?

(a) the total number of solar projects sanctioned, awarded and commissioned under the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Urja Suraksha evam Utthaan Mahabhiyan (PM-KUSUM) scheme since its inception, component-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) the number of projects which have been cancelled, terminated or withdrawn during the same period, component-wise and State/UT-wise, along with the reasons for such cancellations; and
(c) the total solar capacity (in MW) affected due to such cancellations and the percentage of cancelled projects vis-à-vis total projects sanctioned under the scheme?

(a) key recommendations made by NITI Aayog regarding role of Carbon Capture, Utilisation, Storage (CCUS) in decarbonising India’s economy, including sectors targeted and priorities identified;
(b) decisions taken at 25th PM-STIAC meeting to operationalise NITI Aayog’s CCUS recommendations;
(c) measures that NITI Aayog is taking to enhance stakeholder consultations including with States/UTs, industry partners, academia, international collabourators in formulating, implementing policies on SMRs, CCUS; and
(d) quantitative expected outcomes of SMR deployment and CCUS adoption identified by NITI Aayog in terms of: (i) additional clean energy capacity (in GW) expected by 2030 and 2047, (ii) estimated reduction in carbon emissions?

(a) the details of the total area of crops affected or lost (in acres) due to drought, flood, hailstorm, unseasonal rainfall and other natural calamities since 2020-21, State-wise, year-wise;
(b) the total amount of claims/compensation paid under PMFBY, RWBCIS, NDRF/SDRF during the said period, year-wise, State-wise, scheme-wise;
(c) total amount released by Central Government and State Governments under each scheme, year-wise, State-wise;
(d) the total amount pending under each scheme, year-wise, State-wise; and
(e) the number of beneficiaries and total insured area (in acres) covered under each scheme, year-wise and State-wise?

(a) the area of forest land diverted for non-forestry purposes in the country during the last five years, State-wise;
(b) the forest land approved for diversion between 1st April, 2021 and 31st March, 2025, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) the details of such diversions purpose-wise, including infrastructure, mining, power, irrigation, roads, railways, defence and industrial projects; and
(d) the number of proposals approved, rejected and pending during the above period?

(a) the State-wise details of Tribal Freedom Fighters’ Museums sanctioned across the country during last five years indicating year of sanction, approved cost and present status;
(b) the number of such museums that have been completed and inaugurated so far, State-wise; 
(c) the details of museums still under construction and those remaining at DPR stage, despite lapse of several years, State-wise;
(d) the time-bound schedule fixed for completion of each remaining museum, State-wise; and
(e) year-wise Budget Estimates (BE), Revised Estimates (RE), Actual Expenditure (AE) incurred under the scheme for construction of Tribal Freedom Fighters’ Museums during last five years till date?

(a) the year-wise production and consumption of key fertilizers in terms of quantity including Urea, DAP, MOP and NPK, across all States and Union Territories during the last three years;
(b) the current State-wise availability of these fertilizers, including quantity in stock and shortages reported;
(c) the year-wise Maximum Retail Prices and Subsidy rates provided under the Nutrient Based Subsidy (NBS) Scheme; and
(d) the year-wise quantity and value (in INR) of fertilizer imports into the country during 2023–2025, including a breakup of imports by major supplier countries?

(a) the details of CSR expenditure by public and private sector companies during the last five years, including names of companies and projects undertaken, State-wise and year-wise;
(b) the status of implementation and completion of these CSR projects, with details of funds spent, unspent funds and timelines for ongoing projects;
(c) the mechanisms in place for monitoring and evaluating the impact and outcomes of CSR projects, steps taken to ensure effective utilisation of funds for intended purposes; and
(d) whether the Ministry has plans to enhance transparency and reporting under CSR, especially regarding unspent CSR funds and performance of implementing agencies and the details thereof?

(a) year-wise number of coal workers declared medically unfit for continued service, subsidiary-wise, in Coal India Limited (CIL) and its subsidiaries during the last five years;
(b) number of deaths of coal workers including fatal mine accidents and non-accidental deaths, reported during the said period, subsidiary-wise;
(c) existing provisions and clauses under NCWA and other statutory rules governing medical unfitness, compensation, death benefits and compassionate ground employment of coal workers; and
(d) number of dependents provided employment on compassionate grounds, year-wise and subsidiary-wise for the above period?

(a) whether certain private sector employers are failing to deposit both the employer’s share and the employee’s share of PF contributions into EPFO account;
